{
  "summary": "Speeds up functional test execution by waking `wait_until_helper_internal` immediately on P2P message delivery or connection state changes using a `threading.Condition` instead of sleeping 50ms between polls. Also sets `noban_tx_relay = True` in three wallet tests to avoid transaction relay delays.",
  "problem": "Functional tests spend unnecessary time idle due to a fixed 50ms polling interval when waiting on P2P messages and events, and some wallet tests unnecessarily incur default transaction relay rate-limiting delays.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author benchmarks report functional test suite wall time falling from 110.8s to 99.1s (-11% at -j=18) and accumulated CPU time falling from 1715s to 1411s (-17.5%).",
    "Individual test runtimes decreased dramatically: `feature_maxuploadtarget` from 57.9s to 6.2s, `wallet_conflicts` from 49.2s to 7.0s, and `p2p_sendheaders` from 31.1s to 6.8s (author PR description)."
